                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The Dizzy-styled puzzles are great; the only wild puzzle being [spoiler] a guy using a blowtorch lets you use it if you give him a newspaper. [/spoiler] Most puzzles have dialogue and descriptions to hint at their solutions, which makes it very pleasant to play.  The bigger sticking points are if the player doesn't notice there are dark background vines to climb or blocks to destroy.\n\nCompared to its freeware original, the new dungeons are fun, but the added enemies and HP provide little to the experience.",
